Thank you again for your help!
I ran this model:
CFAmodel <- 'cognitivebehavioral =~ AAT_bias_smoking + IAT_app_av_score + IAT_val_score # in my first post, I forgot to add  IAT_val_score, sorry for confusion

             EMG =~ EMGcorr_score + EMGzygo_score + EMGstartle_score

             fMRI =~ ACC + rThal + rStriatum + lSTG + lAG

             sensitization =~ cognitivebehavioral + EMG + fMRI
            '

CFAmodel_a <- cfa(CFAmodel, data_CFA, estimator = "MLR", missing = "FIML")
And receive the error message:
Warning message: In lavaan::lavaan(model = CFAmodel, data = data_CFA, estimator = "MLR", : lavaan WARNING: the optimizer warns that a solution has NOT been found!

and also:

CFAmodel_a <- cfa(CFAmodel, data_CFA, estimator = "MLR", missing = "FIML", std.lv <http://std.lv> = TRUE)

Warning messages: 1: In lav_model_vcov(lavmodel = lavmodel, lavsamplestats = lavsamplestats, : lavaan WARNING: Could not compute standard errors! The information matrix could not be inverted. This may be a symptom that the model is not identified. 2: In lav_test_yuan_bentler(lavobject = NULL, lavsamplestats = lavsamplestats, : lavaan WARNING: could not invert information matrix needed for robust test statistic 3: In lav_object_post_check(object) : lavaan WARNING: some estimated ov variances are negative

Indeed, I have lots of missing data, because the fMRI assessment was only done by a subsample (n=113). Also EMGstartle_score has many missings (observations: n=180). The number of complete cases for all measures is N=60 of a total of N=362. I hope I answered all questions, I also got confused from the messages ;)

Best, Franziska

On Tuesday 9 April 2024 at 17:28:35 UTC+2 danielmo...@gmail.com wrote:
> It seems like my first message didn't get through (or it doesn't appear in the message list in the Google group at least). My last one may seem cryptic if so... This is what I was saying:
>
> The only part that is (locally) underidentified is the "cognitivebehavioral" latent variable, as it is measured by only two indicators. So you need to add a restriction as you correctly did to one of the parameters, i.e. fixing the loading of AAT_bias_smoking to 1. The rest of the fixed parameters may be adding to many restrictions that the fitted model cannot properly accommodate.
>
> You can try freeing those parameters and leaving only the restriction needed for identification, i.e.:
>
> CFAmodel <- 'cognitivebehavioral =~ 1*AAT_bias_smoking + IAT_app_av_score
>              EMG =~ EMGcorr_score + EMGzygo_score + EMGstartle_score
>              fMRI =~ ACC + lAG + rThal + rStriatum + lSTG
>              sensitization =~ cognitivebehavioral + EMG + fMRI'
>
> Hope that helps!
>
> --
