Hi Roger,

You have changed the variable names in the model syntax as suggested. Did you also rename the variable names in the datasets (df, Df, and DF)?

Moreover, *right after* you got the error message on missing observerd variables, type this:

cat(specmod)

This checks whether you have updated specmod as expected. The error message suggests that it still sees "ROA Derivativeuse" in specmod.

Last, lavaan::sem() expects only one object assigned to `data`. Is multigroup model what you really want to fit? What do you mean when you said you wanted to fit to three datasets?

Hope this helps.

-- Shu Fai

